      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Character Sheet Cleanup\n\nA Seedance reference should show **one readable face**. This edit removes the head from the front full-body panel of a three-panel sheet, so the close-up is the only face.\n\n1. Load your sheet (for example the output of the **Character Sheet** template).\n2. Check the **Head box**. The default covers the head of the middle panel of a 16:9 sheet. If a face remains, widen it or replace the numbers with coordinates from your annotation tool (0 to 999 scale: x1 y1 x2 y2).\n3. Run. The original stays untouched, so compare both before you use the new one.\n\nIf the back panel also shows a face, run it again with the box moved to that panel.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Character Sheet Cleanup\n\nA Seedance reference should show **one readable face**. This edit removes the head from the front full-body panel of a three-panel sheet, so the close-up is the only face.\n\n1. Load your sheet (for example the output of the **Character Sheet** template).\n2. Check the **Head box**. The default covers the head of the middle panel of a 16:9 sheet. If a face remains, widen it or replace the numbers with coordinates from your annotation tool (0 to 999 scale: x1 y1 x2 y2).\n3. Run. The original stays untouched, so compare both before you use the new one.\n\nIf the back panel also shows a face, run it again with the box moved to that panel.\n\nBefore the first run, add your ModelArk API key in **Settings > BytePlus**. No other key is needed."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
